            This lecture-recital will balance these questions against an exploration of rhetorical intent behind repetition and variation, Bach’s published thoughts on the matter, and own experiments of performing Mozart’s sonatas on a Stein fortepiano as the instrument that in 1777 became crucial in the professional life of a maturing improviser and composer.
},
 publisher = {},
 title = {Lecture-recital: “Bis repetita placent: C. P. E. Bach, W. A. Mozart, and the Practice of Varied Reprises”},
